<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Ag Ministry estimates grain crop outputs.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Ag Ministry estimates grain crop outputs.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agriculture Ministry estimated grain production for its 1996-1997 Fall-Winter harvest cycles, in a recent report obtained by Reuters.</p>
<p>The ministry forecast output for basic grains in the 1996-1997 fall-winter season, using its most recent estimates from April 1997.</p>
<p>The following are the ministry's crop estimates and comparative figures from the year-ago period.</p>
<p>		1996-1997 Fall-Winter*     1995-1996 Fall-Winter</p>
<p>    Rice		42,400 tonnes		  36,400 tonnes</p>
<p>    Bean	     336,000 tonnes		 286,000 tonnes</p>
<p>    Corn	   3.997 million tonnes		3.16 million tonnes</p>
<p>    Wheat	  3.218 million tonnes		2.87 million tonnes</p>
<p>    Sesame Seed	6,800 tonnes		   6,700 tonnes</p>
<p>    Cotton	    41,400 tonnes		  93,900 tonnes</p>
<p>    Safflower	151,100 tonnes		 181,600 tonnes</p>
<p>    Soy Bean	   3,600 tonnes		     100 tonnes</p>
<p>    Barley	   181,600 tonnes		 132,400 tonnes</p>
<p>    Sorghum	2.407 million tonnes		2.31 million tonnes</p>
<p>  Total	   10.385 million tonnes		9.07 million tonnes</p>
<p>*estimated figures</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
